Third-party notices

This repository holds modelling, retrieval, ranking and verification code only.
No clinical record, no plaque image volume and no subject-level outcome table is
redistributed here. The resources the code reads are named in dataset_urls.txt
with their access terms; the attributions below keep the origin of every
external input visible.

1. Private multi-centre carotid plaque cohort (Layer i); Sites A, B and C across
   Regions I and II. Not redistributed and not obtainable from a public
   repository. Held under a data-usage statement issued by the corresponding
   author, and reported in the manuscript as irreversibly anonymised before
   analysis. The release ships a schema-compatible cohort fixture so that every
   mechanism stays executable without it; see README section 3.

2. Therapeutics Data Commons (TDC), Caco2_Wang task (N = 906 compounds).
   Distributed through the PyTDC client, MIT licence, https://tdcommons.ai/ .
   Role here: auxiliary permeability-class supervision for the molecular branch
   and the assay-endpoint comparison. TDC also redistributes the underlying
   public measurements, whose original sources retain their own terms.

3. OCHEM curated Caco-2 release (9,402 measurements filtered to 5,481 compounds,
   cluster-stratified 4,386/1,095 split), https://ochem.eu/ . Role here: the
   stress out-of-distribution assay endpoint.

4. MoleculeNet, 17 datasets (11 used), MIT licence,
   https://doi.org/10.1039/c7sc02664a . Role here: fusion-depth comparator
   reference for the multimodal baselines.

5. Open Graph Benchmark, ogbg-molhiv and ogbg-molpcba, https://ogb.stanford.edu/
   . Role here: cross-benchmark molecular check on the official splits.

6. ChEMBL (release page updated 2026-05-01; 2,921,148 compounds, 24,527,044
   activities), https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/ , CC BY-SA 3.0. Role here:
   compound-context retrieval service.

7. PubChem, https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ . Role here: structure and
   property context retrieval.

8. BindingDB, https://www.bindingdb.org/ . Role here: binding-measure context
   retrieval.

9. ADMET-AI, Swanson, K. et al. Bioinformatics 40, btae416 (2024),
   https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btae416 , MIT licence. Role here:
   molecular-property comparator that itself consumes the TDC ADMET group; it is
   a comparator and not an independent data source.

10. LIT-PCBA (15 targets), https://drugdesign.unistra.fr/LIT-PCBA/ , and DUD-E
    (102 targets), http://dude.docking.org/ . Tran-Nguyen, V.-K. et al. J. Chem.
    Inf. Model. 60, 4263-4273 (2020). Role here: realistic and idealised virtual
    screening controls.

11. IMPROVE drug-response benchmark, https://github.com/JDACS4C-IMPROVE/ . Role
    here: split construction only; no feature is ingested from it.

12. Carotid Vessel Wall Segmentation and Atherosclerosis Diagnosis Challenge
    (MICCAI 2022), Zenodo records 6481870 (training) and 6843257 (testing),
    CC BY 4.0. Role here: encoder pretraining only. Neither record carries the
    cohort outcomes analysed in the manuscript.

13. Software dependencies are consumed as installed packages and are not
    vendored: PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), SciPy
    (BSD-3-Clause), scikit-learn (BSD-3-Clause) and PyYAML (MIT). Their licences
    apply to those packages, not to this repository.
